css : is cascading style sheets used to style html elements on a web page.
3 types of css  are
1 inline css (inside an html element using the style attribute)
2 internal css (inside a <style> tag in the head section of an html document)
3 external css (in a separate .css file linked to the html document)


selectors:
declaration {
    property : value;
}
table { border :1px solid #c00;}

selectors are divided into 5 categories
1 simple selectors (select elements based on name, id, class)
2 combinators (select elements based on a specific relationship between them)
3 pseudo-classes (select elements based on their state)
4 pseudo-elements (select and style a part of an element)
5 attribute selectors (select elements based on an attribute or attribute value)


when id selectors are used for property we use # before the id name
when class selectors are used for property we use . before the class name